{title: Our Mouths Were Filled With Laughter}
{subtitle: Psalm 126}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 130}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Gm] | [C] | [Bb] [A] | ×2
| [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
When the Lord restored the fortunes [C]of Zion
We were [Dm]like those who dream
Then our mouths were filled with laughter
And our [C]tongues with shouts of joy
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The Lord has [Dm]done great things for us
And we are glad, we are glad
The Lord has done great things [Gm]for [C]us
[Bb]And we [A]are [Dm]glad
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Those who sow in tears
Shall reap with shouts of joy
[Gm]He who goes out weeping, [C]bearing seed
Shall come home [Bb]with shouts [A]of joy, bring[Dm]ing his sheaves
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The Lord has done great things for us
And we are glad, we are glad
The Lord [Gm]has done great things for [C]us
And we [Bb]are [A][Dm]glad
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
